{"title":"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Amelia has a coin that lands heads with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cca6779159e39b9869a54a55f65827014c8e71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"18\" height=\"38\" />, and Blaine has a coin that lands on heads with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Amelia and Blaine alternately toss their coins until someone gets a head; the first one to get a head wins. All coin tosses are independent. Amelia goes first. The probability that Amelia wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347a1d5586e82c832f61ea799d89945ed2837fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0fd869078478f66f2c1e7b9b44c80bf0bfb34e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9959d47fffb760b6cf89894df252b99436e4d8f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the probability Amelia wins. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c705e83cfc097fe6b13c3cbb8d5f394b6aea63ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\text{chance she wins on her first turn} + \\text{chance she gets to her turn again}\\cdot P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"567\" height=\"15\" />, since if she gets to her turn again, she is back where she started with probability of winning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The chance she wins on her first turn is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. The chance she makes it to her turn again is a combination of her failing to win the first turn - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and Blaine failing to win - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Multiplying gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a086f7f990b659b2c3ff6f2ccc7957acdf020bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P = \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2}{5}P\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6d22a6f0e7c51bb3a0e28de7d95fcbfa047312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"37\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb96d35823339c5040ee15da2ddaf69983eddc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-5=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"120\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the probability Amelia wins. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/75422f90fd80d983ad0ec3029088a29bb71c604c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\text{chance she wins on her first turn} + \\text{chance she gets to her second turn}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} + \\text{chance she gets to her third turn}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"892\" height=\"38\" /> This can be represented as an infinite geometric series: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bbd77f6a3b85fd5453e8cf9a09caaa0deae6542.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P=\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{1-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{1-\\frac{2}{5}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{\\frac{3}{5}} = \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{3} = \\frac{5}{9}.\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"47\" /> \nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6d22a6f0e7c51bb3a0e28de7d95fcbfa047312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"37\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/44158592b51323b7ee31f8212e6d1f3b28a98b70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-5 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"123\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>Solution by ktong\n</p><p>~minor LaTeX edit by virjoy2001\n~quicky grammar edit by NSAoPS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can solve this by using 'casework,' the cases being:\nCase 1: Amelia wins on her first turn.\nCase 2 Amelia wins on her second turn.\nand so on.\n</p><p>The probability of her winning on her first turn is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e6261a9b57684fff897400a639b5fe3b2d282c00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. The probability of all the other cases is determined by the probability that Amelia and Blaine all lose until Amelia's turn on which she is supposed to win. So, the total probability of Amelia winning is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd3aac0ef564cc62e876837dc600d3ebbd5a918.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{3}+\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\cdot\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{3}+\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\cdot\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{3}+\\cdots.\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"46\" />\nFactoring out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e6261a9b57684fff897400a639b5fe3b2d282c00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> we get a geometric series:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/effc694b3ac680f3ef387c09e1c0506f75e0b1c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(1+\\dfrac{2}{5}+\\left(\\dfrac{2}{5}\\right)^2+\\cdots\\right) = \\dfrac{1}{3}\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{3/5} = \\boxed{\\dfrac59}.\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Extracting the desired result, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478d01f2c8ca727b666edf6a0b8d42d6e335a91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-5 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"122\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-ConfidentKoala4\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IRyWOZQMTV8?t=4552\">https://youtu.be/IRyWOZQMTV8?t=4552</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=umr2Aj9ViOA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=umr2Aj9ViOA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A\">2017 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017022837\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 242/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5588/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.319      1 -total\n 54.61%    7.819      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 44.53%    6.376      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15389:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017022837 and revision id 287774. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}